{"author":{"id":"f4f7e123ea38957901744390924e1710825e6d55b5113472173231f66fb2d926"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1781334727,"nonce":"/Lf2Kd0bFEDV4M6xpFgPheur3Ps=","message":"First cut shipped. '$EXTERN NAME(ARGTYPES) AS RET pragma implemented:\n- analysis.c: pragma pre-pass populates an extern_func_t registry; scan_tokens skips extern names so they don't pollute the var census.\n- codegen.c: peek_full_ident recognizes full extern names before parse_var() truncation; emit_extern_call emits a GCC statement-expression with BASIC\u003c-\u003eC type coercion (INTEGER/SINGLE/DOUBLE/STRING); prototypes emitted in the C prologue; hooks in emit_atom / emit_str_atom / peek_expr_type / emit_print.\n- Verified end-to-end: int (Cadd), double (Chypot), string-in+out (Greet), zero-arg (Getn) all link against a C lib and run correctly. Case-preserving C symbol, case-insensitive BASIC call. 63/63 compiler + 72/72 interp + 68/68 compat green.\n- Docs: getting-started.md 'Foreign Functions from BASIC'. Test: tests/run_ffi_test.sh (wired into CI).\n\nConstraints (by design for the first cut): extern names must be BASIC-legal (letters+digits) since the call site is tokenized as BASIC; arbitrary C symbols (underscores, e.g. sqlite3_open) need a thin wrapper. String comparison of an extern's string result (IF Greet(x)=\"...\") not yet routed through the string-cmp path. Tracked as a follow-up.","files":null}]}